# ACT SERVICE — COMPLETE PRODUCTION APP & SUPABASE INTEGRATION PROMPT

## 1. Project Mission

Upgrade the existing Act Service application into a fully functional, database-connected application using Supabase.

**Application name: Act Service**

This is a private personal-care application featuring menstrual cycle tracking, daily mood and symptom tracking, vegetarian food selection and booking, a “Ring the Bell” feature, and a separate administrator dashboard.

This is not a demo prototype. Implement working authentication, persistent database storage, authorization, database migrations, real request processing, and live updates.

Preserve the existing romantic, polished, mobile-first design. Do not unnecessarily redesign working screens or remove existing features.

### Non-negotiable requirements

- Integrate the application with a real Supabase project.
- Remove all demo credentials and mock authentication.
- Remove every User/Admin selection option from the login screen.
- Automatically redirect authenticated users according to their verified account role.
- Never display the Admin Control Panel inside the user interface.
- Start all personal tracking sections without dummy activity records.
- Start the cart, favourites, notifications, and request history empty.
- Store actual user-generated records in Supabase.
- Never expose Supabase secret or service-role credentials in frontend code.
- Enable and verify appropriate Row Level Security (RLS) policies.
- Do not display prices or payment information in food ordering.

