## 15. Real-Time Updates and Phone Notifications

Use Supabase Realtime for appropriate database-driven updates.

When the user submits a food request or rings the bell:
1. Save the request to Supabase.
2. Generate a corresponding administrator notification through the secure server-side workflow.
3. Make the request visible to the authorized administrator.
4. Update the administrator dashboard without requiring a manual refresh where Realtime is supported.

When the administrator changes a request status, update the user's request view using authorized database reads or Realtime subscriptions.

Use RLS to restrict Realtime events to the appropriate audience. Do not broadcast private database events publicly.

For actual Android phone push notifications, implement a trusted server-side integration with Firebase Cloud Messaging or the chosen supported push provider, after its required credentials and Android configuration are supplied.

Do not claim a phone push notification was delivered simply because a database row was created.

Provide clear handling of notification permissions, device registration, delivery errors, and unavailable push configuration.

The application must remain functional even if push notifications have not yet been configured.

